I got something for you, Mai.

251
00:17:29,420 --> 00:17:30,340
Up high!

252
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:31,890
Huh?

253
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,080
It's all right, Mai. I'm right here.

254
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:43,320
What are you doing?

255
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:44,920
Saving your life, Mike.

256
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:47,190
All right.

257
00:17:47,273 --> 00:17:48,103
See you around.

258
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,150
Take care.

259
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,110
Congratulations.

260
00:17:52,193 --> 00:17:53,023
You win.

261
00:17:58,460 --> 00:17:59,560
Joey, no!

262
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,760
You're wrong.

263
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:07,786
I never attacked, so you
didn't lose the duel.

264
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:11,220
But I'm too exhausted to finish.

265
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:14,500
I won't let the Orikalkos
take you away, Joey.

266
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:16,973
It's too late for that.

267
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:20,501
I already lost a duel, so
there's no turning back.

268
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:26,457
I'm just glad that if one of us had to lose
our soul, it didn't have to be you, Mai.

269
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:27,640
Don't say that!

270
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:34,500
Hey, Mai, that was one of the greatest
duels I ever fought. Thank you.

271
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:39,390
Joey!

272
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,490
No!

273
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:45,580
She's been set free!

274
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:48,960
Ah, but what's this?

275
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:52,180
It seems Miss Valentine
has served her purpose.

276
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:55,440
Oh, no! What's wrong?

277
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:56,840
Is it Joey?

278
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,360
I'm afraid so.

279
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:10,260
What's up with Prettius?

280
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,471
There must be some kind of
glitch in the holographic image.

281
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,240
Joey! Wait!

282
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,060
Snap out of it!

283
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:24,560
This is all my fault.

284
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:29,200
I was angry and confused, and I
blamed all my loneliness on you.

285
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,360
So I tried to get rid of you.

286
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:33,620
How could I be so selfish?

287
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:37,020
You're the only one who
ever cared about me.

288
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:43,520
You're the closest friend I ever
had, and how did I repay you?

289
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:46,940
By leaving you for a madman
who promised me power.

290
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:52,980
I'll make him regret the day
he ever met my Valentine.

291
00:19:57,160 --> 00:20:00,700
The only way to fix this is
to meet darts face to face.

292
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,480
Here goes nothing.

293
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:26,580
Cave Darts, is that you?

294
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:28,200
Guess again, Mai.

295
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,590
Huh?

296
00:20:29,673 --> 00:20:30,560
What do you want?

297
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:43,557
no way what happened he lost the duel wait

298
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:48,100
does that mean yes his
soul belongs to darts now
